


# matb3aa lyrics pipeline

Two scripts + orchestrator. Fetches lyrics from matb3aa.com.
No D1 migration, no Worker changes. Writes local JSON only.

## Inputs

| File | Source | Content |
|---|---|---|
| `artists.json` | wrangler dump | `[{ artist_id, artist_name }, ...]` |
| `tracks.json` | wrangler dump | `[{ artist_id, track_name }, ...]` |

## Outputs

| File | Content |
|---|---|
| `search-results.json` | Each track: `{ matched, matb3aaId, ... }` |
| `lyrics-bodies.json` | Each matched track: `{ lyrics, bytes, error }` |

## Step 1 — dump D1

From `E:\matb3aa-game\music-game-wrangler`:
cd E:\matb3aa-game\music-game-wrangler
npx wrangler d1 execute music-game-db --remote --json --command="SELECT id AS artist_id, name AS artist_name FROM artists WHERE tracks_count > 0 ORDER BY name" > ..\server\scripts\matb3aa-lyrics\artists.json
npx wrangler d1 execute music-game-db --remote --json --command="SELECT DISTINCT artist_id, name AS track_name FROM tracks WHERE r2_key IS NOT NULL" > ..\server\scripts\matb3aa-lyrics\tracks.json



## Flags

| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `--artist=65` | Process one artist only |
| `--fresh` | Ignore existing output files, re-fetch everything |

Both scripts resume by default: re-running skips entries already present
with a non-error result in the output JSON.

## How matching works

1. Search matb3aa by track name: `GET /api/v1/search?query={name}&loader=searchPage`
2. Filter results to `result.name === track.name` AND `result.artists[0].id === track.artist_id`
3. If no exact match on page 1, check up to page 3 (some names are common)
4. If still nothing → log as `no-exact-match`, no lyrics fetched
5. For matches: `GET /api/v1/tracks/{id}/lyrics?duration=0`

No fuzzy fallback — a wrong ID means wrong lyrics, which is worse than no lyrics.

## Headers

matb3aa blocks plain requests. Every call sends:
- `User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 ...`
- `Referer: https://www.matb3aa.com/`
- `Origin: https://www.matb3aa.com`

## Rate limit

- Concurrency: 4
- Delay: 400ms between requests per worker
- Retry: 3 attempts with exponential backoff on 429/5xx